Two useful reductions emerged. Once energy-PD gives `p≤1/2`, the identity `e=p(1−p)` can be inverted by a power series with nonnegative coefficients, so positive definiteness of `e` already implies PD of `p`. I’ll use this to optimize an energy profile without breaking the binary identity.

There is also a further necessary condition: covariance matrices of shifted nonnegative high-pass functions are completely positive. This is stronger than entrywise positivity plus PSD in general, so I won’t claim that the two-profile class captures every macroscopic constraint.
